    <h2>Level 111 walkthrough: every move in order<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Steps 1–3</span>
      <strong>Swipe the hair under the bed (then 2 more)</strong>
      <p>Swipe the hair under the bed to the right. Drag the clock to the girl under the bed. Drag the clock to the girl who's working out.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Steps 4–6</span>
      <strong>Swipe the quilt downwards (then 2 more)</strong>
      <p>Swipe the quilt downwards. Drag the clock to the sleeping girl. Drag the clock to the girl reading a horror novel.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Steps 7–9</span>
      <strong>Drag the clock (then 2 more)</strong>
      <p>Drag the clock to the girl who is playing with her phone. Drag the clock to the girl who is studying. Drag the hammer to the crack.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Steps 10–12</span>
      <strong>Drag the clock (then 2 more)</strong>
      <p>Drag the clock to the girl who is digging a tunnel. Swipe left on the door. Drag the clock to the fashionable girl.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>If your level 111 shows “Biased Mother”<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Brain Puzzle 3 does not hand every player the same scene at the same number: builds and
    install order differ, and both variants are on record. If the banner on your screen reads
    “Help her live a good life.”, this is that scene, 19 moves in order:</p>
    <ol class="alt-steps">
        <li>You can't directly drag the money if the defamation issue hasn't been resolved.</li>
